      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given that $k\\ge 0$ is an integer, $\\frac{{((k+1)!)}^{2}}{k!}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n(k+1)!=(k+1)k!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $k!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{((k+1)!)}^{2}}{k!} & =\\frac{{((k+1)k!)}^{2}}{k!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k+1)^{2}\\,\\cdot (k!)^{2}}{k!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k+1)^{2}\\,\\cdot k!\\cdot \\cancel{k!}}{\\cancel{k!}} \\\\  & =(k+1)^{2}k!\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
